silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_04_type_as_kleisli_arrow_decomposition_step_2__step_gate;_admit;_type^kl_=_admit_o_gate a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "gate is a predicate that asks: is this witness naming an olog object (TypedNode) or an olog arrow (TypedArrow) or neither (bot)? admit is the step that, when gate says yes, produces the TypedLeg. The full type operation = admit composed after gate." .
